Some amino acids in collagen can be modified to improve the stability of the protein. For example, the amino acid lysine can be modified to form hydroxylysine.

Fig. 2.1 shows a disaccharide bonded to the amino acid hydroxylysine in a collagen molecule. The disaccharide is made from two monosaccharides, which are indicated by the labels **D** and **E** in Fig. 2.1.

{{figure:figure_2_1.png}}
